ng","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLScaling","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLScaling","abstract":[{"text":"Margins, page sizes, and distances are all measured in tenths to keep MusicXML data in a consistent coordinate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system as much as possible. The translation to absolute units is done with the scaling type, which specifies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how many millimeters are equal to how many tenths. For a staff height of 7 mm, millimeters would be set to 7","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while tenths is set to 40. The ability to set a formula rather than a single scaling factor helps avoid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"roundoff errors.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"}}}